## 5. Extended Research: Pairwise vs. Full Three-Layer Coupling

### 5.1 The Extended Research Question
> **"Does pairwise dependency analysis adequately predict cascade behavior when all three infrastructure layers (Road, Power, Water) interact simultaneously, or does simultaneous interaction create higher-order / synergistic cascade behavior?"**

To address this without bias or artificial amplification, we implemented the full **8-level Coupling Hierarchy (M0 through M7)**:

| Model | Power $\rightarrow$ Water (D1) | Power $\rightarrow$ Road (D2) | Water $\rightarrow$ Road (D3) | Coupling Configuration | Purpose |
|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|---|---|
| **M0** | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | None | Independent baseline |
| **M1** | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | P $\rightarrow$ W only | Pairwise coupling |
| **M2** | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ | P $\rightarrow$ R only | Pairwise coupling |
| **M3** | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | W $\rightarrow$ R only | Pairwise coupling |
| **M4** | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ | P $\rightarrow$ W + W $\rightarrow$ R | Two-dependency combination |
| **M5** | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | P $\rightarrow$ R + W $\rightarrow$ R | Two-dependency combination |
| **M6** | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | P $\rightarrow$ W + P $\rightarrow$ R | Two-dependency combination |
| **M7** | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | P $\rightarrow$ W + P $\rightarrow$ R + W $\rightarrow$ R | **Full Three-Layer Coupling** |

